From 14bb69aa8de7e15a807b6cae4852578a105fbfa9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "A.R." <boldaxolotl@proton.me>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] Fix firmware test build errors

Several firmware tests in src/integration/test_suites fail to compile or
link at this revision with GCC 14 or later (Booley's RISC-V Sandbox ships
xPack GCC 15.2):

- iccm_hash.h: declare wait_pcr5_ready(), which iccm_hash.c defines and
  the directed ICCM-hash tests call.
- pv_hash_reset: define the interrupt-counter struct its ISR header
  expects, and use the renamed SHA512_GEN_PCR_HASH_NONCE_0 register.
- smoke_test_hmac_errortrigger, smoke_test_kv_ecc_flow1/2: these files
  call srand() without including <stdlib.h>, an implicit declaration
  that GCC 14+ rejects. The tests draw from xorshift32(), so seed it with
  xorshift32_init() instead. smoke_test_kv_crypto_flow2 gets the same
  seeding change.
- smoke_test_kv_crypto_flow2: give ML-DSA keygen a full-size private-key
  buffer instead of passing a single word where an array is expected.
- smoke_test_kv_ecdh_flow: add the missing void return type to
  kv_aes_flow().
- smoke_test_hw_config, smoke_test_ras: make service_soc_ifc_notif_intr()
  static inline; a plain C99 inline function has no external definition,
  so any call the compiler does not inline fails to link.

Test-only change; no RTL is touched.
